  "summary": "Scottsdale Mayor Lisa Borowsky is pushing the city council to review the Scottsdale Police Department's use of Flock ALPR cameras, citing resident concerns. A council agenda item could schedule a presentation and possible action on the 85-camera program for the Oct. 20 meeting, while police defend the system as an effective, policy-bound investigative tool.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Borowsky is asking the council to review the city's use of Flock cameras.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock cameras came to Scottsdale in 2023, and today there are 85 citywide, but Borowsky wants current council members to have a say in the program's future.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "Our ALPR program is not a mass surveillance system and is not used in that way. It is subject to strict policies, retention limits, and oversight.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "If passed, Tuesday's agenda item would put a presentation, discussion and possible action on the entire ALPR program on Scottsdale City Council's Oct. 20 meeting.",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    }
  ],
